      "B_configuration": "Constructs mixed membership and broader replication-worker set.",
      "B_leader_epoch": "Acquires authority and supplies competing lease/stepdown protection.",
      "B_client": "Public VerifyLeader contract motivates use for avoiding stale reads."
    },
    "obligation_relation_kind": "establishment",
    "counterevidence": [
      "Commitment uses only voter match indexes and lease checks explicitly count only voters.",
      "Any negative registered response can cause failure; leader exit fails pending verification.",
      "Lease timeout may end the relevant window; nonvoter presence alone does not show stale data or an elected successor."
    ],
    "unknowns": [
      "Clarify the exact applicable authority guarantee of VerifyLeader and whether independently grounded eligibility suffices for a scoped obligation.",
      "Construct legal membership/leadership history and controlled transport schedule that observes which peers supply positive replies while preserving lease and negative-response paths."
    ],
    "priority": 3,
    "trigger_rationale": "The producer set differs from both the voter-derived threshold and explicit voter filters in commitment/lease code. Trace and a smaller isolated check can distinguish an accounting discrepancy; a full stale-read claim additionally needs a correlated successor election and endpoint. Snapshot-age and vote-persistence leads require more fault/history investigation, so verification has the most concrete current discriminator."
